creening, and efficacy tracking. The company incorporates Prolaio's cardiovascular data collection and analytics platform, which includes FDA-cleared algorithms and high-density patient data, to support drug development and clinical intelligence. The company engages in strategic in-licensing and acquisitions to expand its pipeline of targeted treatments. Kardigan serves biopharmaceutical companies, cardiovascular researchers, and healthcare providers in the cardiology sector. The company was formerly known as EnCarda, Inc. and changed its name to Kardigan, Inc. in December 2024. The company was founded in 2023 and is based in Princeton, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Tassos Anastasios E. Gianakakos M.Sc., MBA | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Chairman | Age 52 | Compensation: $5.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 241 people. Stock-based compensation of $66K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Kardigan, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.5B market cap on $0 of annual revenue.","The company is burning through $158M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -10.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","Net dilution runs at 31.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 294% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber"